AB  - The Jingkou Double-Track Railway Bridge carrying a section of the Chengdu-Chongqing Middle Line High-speed Railway intersects with piers No. 23 and No. 24 of the existing Shanghai-Chengdu Railway, The design adopts the plan of girder jack-up and pier replacement, which constructs new portal piers at the original pier location of the existing Shanghai-Chengdu Railway to support, remove, and replace the existing piers. To ensure that the operations which could be completed within the 31. 5 h window time and minimize the disruption to the service of the Shanghai-Chengdu Railway, the innovative research has been conducted on a deep integration of BIM, GIS, BIM + FEM, AI, IoT, virtual construction, and image recognition technologies, the platform of girder jack-up and pier replacement intelligent construction technology integrates BIM deepening modeling, train warning, key technologies for intelligent construction, video monitoring, and information management. To shorten the construction time during construction, it is divided into two special construction processes: the out-window-time and in-window-time stages. The coming trains of the Shanghai-Chengdu Railway are early warned by a train proximity early warning system combined with an electronic fence, it ensures the safety of the construction. By utilizing various monitoring methods such as strain sensors, laser displacement sensors, and fully automatic measurement robots, data is automatically transmitted to the BIM model-based digital twin platform for girder jack-up and pier replacement. This platform provides the thresholds、warnings and automatic adjustments for construction processes such as T-beam lifting, steel beam slippage, and offset adjustment, achieving construction efficiency. The progress is visible, measurable, and controllable, which achieves fast and intelligent construction without affecting the normal operation of existing railway lines. © 2025 Wuhan Bridge Media Co., Ltd., MBEC. All rights reserved.
