AB  - Construction load of adjacent works is the additional load imposed on existing underground structures due to the disturbance of the adjacent works construction. Such load may cause structural damages or even failure of existing underground structures, threatening the urban safety. However, it is still unclear how the construction load of adjacent works evolves. To probe this problem, it is required to uncover the coupling mechanism among the adjacent works, stratum, and existing structures, but an effective experimental method is still unavailable up to now. Hence, a digital twin-based experimental method was proposed for construction loads of adjacent works. In this method, the digital twin technology and hybrid simulation technology are combined to overcome the difficulty in fidelity of numerical model in traditional hybrid simulation technology, so that the laboratory investigation for the construction loads of adjacent works can be realized. Moreover, two interactive update modules were developed for data exchange among the physical space of the construction site, the digital twin, and the physical model test of stratum structure. Furthermore, a system architecture was established for the digital twin-based experimental method. With the proposed system architecture applied to the project cases, its feasibility is preliminarily validated. © 2022 Editorial Office of China Civil Engineering Journal. All rights reserved.
