AB  - The prefabricated building is one important way to transform traditional construction mode to modern industrial mode. Digital twinning can be used as the key technology to realize the goal of intelligent construction. Applying digital twin to the construction stage is the key strategy to improve the informationization and intelligence of construction process of prefabricated building. For this reason, an implementation of digital twin framework in the construction management was proposed. From the perspective of physical construction site entity modeling, digital twin virtual body modeling and virtual-real interaction modeling, the spatial dimension modeling theory of assembly construction process based on digital twin was put forward. Further, the theory of spatio-temporal evolution data modeling was studied. Evolutionary modeling method and massive data association modeling method of assembly construction process were proposed. The proposed digital twin modeling method was applied and verified by the case of hoisting safety risk management in assembly construction process. The solution proves the feasibility and effectiveness of the modeling method and improves the level of informatization and intelligence in assembly hoisting process. It also provides a new idea for the development of digital twin theory in the construction industry. © 2021, Editorial Office of Journal of Building Structures. All right reserved.
