AD  - Fujian Shimenno Port Construction and Development Co., Ltd, Putian, 351152, China
AB  - Structural safety assessment is an important means to ensure the safe operation and maintenance of civil engineering structures, However, conventional planned maintenance strategies suffer from a low degree of informatization and rely on experience for decision-making. Thus, this paper presents a digital twin-driven structural safety assessment method applicable to civil engineering structures during the operation and maintenance phase. Firstly, according to the structural service scenarios, the digital twin framework with 5 levels of structural safety assessment is proposed, and the functions of each part are elaborated in details. Secondly, three key technologies for the construction of digital twin models and multimodal twin data, a data interaction network and a structural safety assessment method are summarized. Finally, taking a truss structure as an example, the digital twin-driven structural safety assessment platform is established, whose feasibility and effectiveness are verified. The construction of multimodal twin data can be implemented using the Latin hypercube sampling and parametric modeling techniques. The real-time data interaction component is achieved by a serial port protocol and a TCP protocol. The surrogate model can implement prediction of structural response. Bayesian-based structural safety assessment method can accurately infer the failure probability of the structure. The digital twin-driven structural safety assessment method achieves accurate structural prediction and decision-making, while the results can provide feedback and control over the operation and maintenance of physical entities. © 2025, Chinese Society of Civil Engineering. All rights reserved.
