AB  - Intelligent construction is revolutionizing how bridges are designed, constructed and maintained. The key technologies, such as building information modeling(BIM), the Internet of Things (IoT), AI in construction, etc., are changing traditional construction procedures into extremely productive, economical, and environmentally friendly processes. This study categories the key common technologies in the intelligent construction of long-span bridges into four modules; parametric design, virtual construction, intelligent construction and equipment, and intelligent monitoring and control. In parametric design, the utilization of a data-driven BIM forward design method, parametric digital modelling and light weighting technologies improves the design efficiency. In virtual construction, technologies, such as intelligent construction organization, construction procedure modeling, intelligent component size inspection and virtual assembly, digital twin and big data analysis, effectively optimize the construction scheme. The practices of a series of advanced construction techniques and equipment greatly enhance the construction accuracy and efficiency, for instance, the pile intelligent control, robotic spoil removal inside caisson, integrated climbing formwork, intelligent girder erection crane with machine vision guidance, intelligent cable stressing and monitoring. The integrated aerial, airborne, and ground inspection techniques in multiple fields, such as slope inspection, wind, wave and current forecasting, intelligent control of bridge alignment and robot inspection system, ensure the safety and quality of the project. The study offers insights into the intelligent construction of long-span bridges requiring improved efficiency, sustainability and resilience, and reduced environmental effects. © 2025 Wuhan Bridge Media Co., Ltd., MBEC. All rights reserved.
